The fx atlas's staging regression (seen live in the 13 500-unit battle at 4K: minutes of no effects): the keep path chose rects against the 2 MiB allowance, added the ALP index share and staged against the base cap, so a full allowance (2560 KB) never fit and the pass skipped every frame until an atlas reset. Fixed in c2a3066c: staging against FX_STAGE_CAP (base + index quarter + ALP table); an oversize keep goes through the banded whole page. Review verified the arithmetic, the allocation size, the banded fallback's termination and index re-upload. Acted in 7c7ec134: tagpu_vk_stage.h's address-space bound; a device that maps less than FX_STAGE_CAP also takes the banded path (only a device that maps no row still skips; not exercised on a device); effects.md §7.5 in the present tense. Reproduced only by a forced test build (the owner's line on 197ccb6d, none after).
